Missing: Move Function creates the target's header when there is none

When target.c has no header, nothing declares the moved function where it is still
used. Here main() in source.c calls func(), so source.c no longer compiles cleanly
(an implicit declaration). With a target.h, Move Function adds the extern there and
includes it in source.c (test_move_function_to_other_file_with_header_file). This test
asks for the same when target.h does not exist: create it with an include guard and
the extern, and include it in source.c.

Decide first how a new file is made. The protocol has no record for it, so expected
assumes a goto to offset 0 in target.h, which the client opens as a new buffer, and a
replacement that inserts all of it. Move Function to New Module (backlog #87) needs
the same, for the .c too.

When this works, test_move_function_to_other_file changes as well: its expected pins
that no declaration is made.
